// [QL] A test map for R20 / R21 / R22 - surface detail work.
//
// Hand-authored, ours, and committable: Quake Live's own map sources were never
// released, so there is no legitimate way to recompile one of its maps, and a
// recompiled .bsp would be redistributing its content anyway. This is a few
// brushes we wrote, which is neither.
//
// WHAT IT IS FOR, and it is not what it was first asked for. The question was
// whether a map with light entities could be produced to test runtime
// relighting. It can - compile with -keeplights and /maplights will report them
// - but that path is no longer needed: the lightgrid already carries a light
// direction per cell, and what has to vary across a rock is the normal, not the
// light. See R20 in TRACKER.md.
//
// R20 STAGE A is what it now mostly exists for: the row of seven panels against
// the +Y wall, documented where they are declared below. Stage A's one claim a
// build cannot check is that the derived bumps point the right way, and a
// mirrored tangent is invisible on axis-aligned UVs - which every face in the
// first version of this map was. The panels put four rotations, a shear, the
// qlNoPerturb opt-out and a collapsed lightmap-first shader side by side under
// one light, so the answer is a glance rather than a measurement.
//
// What it is otherwise good for is a controlled scene: known geometry, known
// lighting, no dependency on pak00, and small enough to recompile in seconds
// while iterating on shading. And one specific experiment worth running before
// R20 Stage B is built, because Stage B is designed around its outcome:
//
//   compile twice, once with the rock shader carrying q3map_shadeAngle 60 and
//   once without, and compare the lightmaps.
//
// Stage B assumes the faceting on Quake Live's rocks is baked into the lightmap
// by q3map2's per-face lighting, and is designed to stop the lightmap being
// what shapes the surface because of it. If the two compiles look identical
// that assumption is wrong and Stage B needs rethinking before it is written,
// not after.
//
// COMPILING. Use build-testmap.sh next to this file; it stages the filesystem,
// runs the three phases and packs the pk3. The flags it uses and why are in its
// header. Verified with id-tech-3-tools/map-compiler, which builds from source
// with everything vendored, so cmake and a C++ compiler are the whole toolchain:
//
//   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/id-tech-3-tools/map-compiler
//   cmake -S map-compiler -B bld -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release && cmake --build bld -j
//   MAPCOMPILER=./bld/mapcompiler ./content/testmaps/build-testmap.sh
//
// It needs no Quake Live install. The R20 panels use textures/qltest/tangent,
// which is ours and ships in the test pk3; set QLDIR if you want the room's
// ct_ragnarok/rock_03 at its real scale as well.
//
// BSP VERSION. -game quakelive is a stock profile in that compiler and it is
// what makes this a version 47 BSP - nothing has to be patched to get one.
// Our loader takes 46 too (v47 is v46 plus LUMP_ADVERTISEMENTS, see qfiles.h),
// so a -game quake3 build also loads; 47 is what the real maps are, so it is
// what the test should be. Confirmed by reading the header back: IBSP 47.
//
// TWO SILENT TRAPS, both found by compiling rather than by reading:
//
// q3map2 loads ONLY the .shader files named in scripts/shaderlist.txt. Without
// that file the test shaders are never parsed and their panels come out at the
// wrong UV scale, reported as one "Couldn't find image for shader" line. The
// engine has no such list and loads every .shader it finds, so this is a
// compile-time requirement with no run-time symptom to lead you to it.
//
// And the "textures/" prefix rule is INVERTED between the two files. A face in
// this .map writes "qltest/tangent" and q3map2 adds the prefix; a shader block
// in the .shader must be named "textures/qltest/noperturb" in full. Getting it
// wrong in either direction fails the same quiet way.
//
// -keeplights goes on the BSP phase, NOT the light phase. It is parsed in
// bsp.cpp and works by stamping "_keepLights" "1" into worldspawn, which the
// light phase then reads back. Passing it to -light is accepted in silence and
// does nothing - which is exactly what happened the first time, and the lights
// were stripped while the command line looked correct.
//
// LOADING IT. The .bsp has to go in a .pk3, not loose in baseq3/maps/.
//
// A pure client only reads files that live inside a pk3, and the server side
// does not go through that check - so a loose .bsp produces a server that loads
// the map, spawns into it and reports a spawn point, and a renderer that says
//
//   ERROR: RE_LoadWorldMap: couldn't load maps/qltest_light.bsp
//
// which reads like a corrupt or invalid BSP and is nothing of the kind. The
// give-away is CM_LoadMap succeeding a few lines above it and "Connected to a
// pure server" in between.
//
//   cd baseq3 && zip -r qltest.pk3 maps/qltest_light.bsp
//
// sv_pure 0 also works and is worse: it changes what the client will load for
// everything, to avoid packaging one file.
//
// // Add -deluxe to the light phase for a BSP that exercises the deluxemap
// detection in /maplights. No Quake Live map carries them.
//
// COMPILED AND CHECKED, unlike the first version of this file. That version
// produced a 1188-byte BSP with zero surfaces, because every plane was wound
// backwards: q3map2 takes the face normal as (p0-p1) x (p2-p1), so the winding
// used here made every brush inside-out and enclosing nothing. It reported no
// error - an inside-out brush is not invalid, it is just empty. Compiling it
// was the only thing that would have caught that, and the first version of this
// comment said it had not been compiled and left the geometry conservative in
// the hope that would be enough. It was not.
//
// The texture name is also written WITHOUT the "textures/" prefix. q3map2 adds
// it, so a name carrying it becomes textures/textures/... and silently misses.
//
// Texture names are from docs/pak-manifest.txt, not from memory.
// RE_RegisterShader returns 0 for a name the pak does not contain and reports
// nothing, so a guessed name renders nothing and says nothing about it.

// entity 0
{
"classname" "worldspawn"
"message" "QL surface detail test"
// floor
{
( 272 272 0 ) ( 272 -272 0 ) ( -272 -272 0 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
( 272 -272 -16 ) ( 272 272 -16 ) ( -272 272 -16 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
( 272 272 -16 ) ( 272 272 0 ) ( -272 272 0 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
( -272 -272 -16 ) ( -272 -272 0 ) ( 272 -272 0 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
( 272 -272 -16 ) ( 272 -272 0 ) ( 272 272 0 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
( -272 272 -16 ) ( -272 272 0 ) ( -272 -272 0 ) ct_ragnarok/rock_03 0 0 0 0.500000 0.500000 0 0 0
}
